name stress_pose
describe The worst pose measured so far: ground level at a hilltop, shadows and AO on, looking out over the terrain. CLAUDE.md records 76 fps here against 155-159 panoramic, so this -- not the panorama -- is the pose a GPU budget is set from. Used by goals 220 and 221 as the instrumentation-cost measurement pose.
backend both

# TAA off for every scenario that compares a capture against a golden. Measured, not assumed:
# with TAA on, vk-vs-vk moves 0.996% of pixels at this pose against a 1.5% gate, and with it off
# 0.341% -- see dev/harness/src/image_compare.hpp for the full four-case table.
option --no-taa

pose_ground 48,0 -90 -6 1.7
wait 5

capture end stress_pose

assert frames > 0
assert contrast_percent > 6

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ goal 273: the regression gate
# A PERCENTILE of the GPU timestamp range across this fixed camera path, per research section 6.8 --
# never a mean (one hitch moves it) and above all never fps, which this machine's 165 Hz
# FIFO_RELAXED panel caps at 155-159 and which therefore cannot express a regression at all.
#
# PER BACKEND, because vk and d3d12 differ by 30-35% here and `ctest -L scenario` runs vk ONLY. A
# single threshold would have to be set by the slower backend, leaving the faster one 35% of slack
# -- a 30% vk regression would sail straight through the gate that CI actually runs.
#
# Each number is ~1.2x the worst of four runs on THAT backend: the smallest margin that survives
# run-to-run noise and still fails when the budget is tightened by 20%, which is goal 273's own
# Check and is demonstrated in the log.
#   vk    ~817 frames, p95 3.80 3.80 3.82   (0.5% spread)
#   d3d12 ~800 frames, p95 5.05 5.09 5.14 5.21 (3% spread)
assert gpu_ms_p95 < 4.4 vk
assert gpu_ms_p95 < 6.0 d3d12
